From 18d9faf460c24a81d923a5cad033553d3c71c158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:00:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: never self-advertise a WebSocket port as a TCP P2P
 address

GetLocalAddrForPeer() may adopt the address a peer reports seeing us at.
For inbound peers ABC takes that report's port too, since such a peer
reached our listening port. An inbound /p2p/ws peer, however, reached the
HTTP/WebSocket endpoint (-publicbind or the RPC port), so with a routable
address we could advertise IP:<websocket port> as a plain TCP P2P address
and third parties would try P2P against the HTTP server.

For WebSocket peers, take only the reported IP and keep our P2P port, as
for outbound peers. Likewise, if the best local address is the
-externaldomain NET_WSS entry, never pair its wss:// port with an IP.
WebSocket reachability is advertised only through -externaldomain
(NET_WSS over ADDRv2).

The extended get_local_addr_for_peer_port test fails without this change.

Integration adaptation relative to HTTP/WS series-20261019/0009: its inbound-WebSocket condition and regression test already live in the adapted source0003 commit. Retain them there; this commit adds the remaining NET_WSS-domain-to-TCP port correction without a duplicate test or duplicate hunk.
---
 src/net.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/net.cpp b/src/net.cpp
index 1182008bef10f4706c900be34f3b59179ce9588a..7eff43076190924d84865cc047508abfc899cbc4 100644
--- a/src/net.cpp
+++ b/src/net.cpp
@@ -265,7 +265,13 @@ std::optional<CService> GetLocalAddrForPeer(CNode &node) {
             // the peer and leave the port in `addrLocal` as returned by
             // `GetLocalAddress()` above. The peer has no way to observe our
             // listening port when we have initiated the connection.
-            addrLocal.SetIP(node.GetAddrLocal());
+            // The same holds for WebSocket peers: the port they reached is
+            // the HTTP/WebSocket endpoint, not our TCP P2P port. And if the
+            // best local address was a NET_WSS name, its port is that of the
+            // wss:// endpoint, so use our P2P listening port.
+            const uint16_t port{addrLocal.IsWSS() ? GetListenPort()
+                                                  : addrLocal.GetPort()};
+            addrLocal = CService{node.GetAddrLocal(), port};
         }
     }
     if (addrLocal.IsRoutable() || gArgs.GetBoolArg("-addrmantest", false)) {
